G-1). Travel-office approval also doesn't replace manager approval (TRV-2).\n\n**After proceeding:**\n3. **Notify finance within 24 hours of the purchase.** This is a condition of the emergency exception (EMG-1). It is a notification only, not an approval (DEF-2).\n\n**Not required:**\n- **Advance finance approval.** It wouldn't be needed anyway, because $801 is below the $2,500 threshold (EXP-2). It would also be waived because this is a qualifying emergency of $5,000 or less from an approved vendor (EMG-1).\n- **Compliance-officer authorization.** That only applies to prohibited vendors (VEN-1, VEN-2), and this vendor is approved.\n\n**Note:** I've treated the emergency as qualifying because you said it was. If it doesn't meet DEF-1 (an immediate operational or safety risk that can't reasonably wait for normal approval), the emergency exception doesn't apply (EMG-2). Manager and travel-office approval would still be required in advance. The 24-hour finance notification would no longer be required because it comes from the emergency exception.","ttft_ms":2118,"type":"result","duration_ms":16081,"uuid":"67851f88-cbbc-4705-ba42-dedf4bf62fdd","ttft_stream_ms":1894,"time_to_request_ms":135,"first_content_frame_ms":1894,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
